From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:11:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] phy: samsung-ufs: gs101: terminate the pre-HS calibration
 table

samsung_ufs_phy_calibrate() walks a calibration table until it finds an
entry with a zero id, but tensor_gs101_pre_pwr_hs_config[] has no
END_UFS_PHY_CFG. The walk therefore runs into whatever the compiler
placed after the array, typically tensor_gs101_post_pwr_hs_config[],
and programs those values too before the power mode change.

Add the missing terminator so that only the two pre-HS values are
written, matching Google's calib_of_hs_rate_{a,b} tables for gs101.

The table was added with the original gs101 UFS PHY support; this tree's
history is squashed, so there is no commit hash for a Fixes: tag.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/phy/samsung/phy-gs101-ufs.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-gs101-ufs.c b/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-gs101-ufs.c
index a15e1f453..d4af94f3f 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-gs101-ufs.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-gs101-ufs.c
@@ -98,6 +98,7 @@ static const struct samsung_ufs_phy_cfg tensor_gs101_pre_init_cfg[] = {
 static const struct samsung_ufs_phy_cfg tensor_gs101_pre_pwr_hs_config[] = {
 	PHY_TRSV_REG_CFG_GS101(0x369, 0x11, PWR_MODE_ANY),
 	PHY_TRSV_REG_CFG_GS101(0x246, 0x03, PWR_MODE_ANY),
+	END_UFS_PHY_CFG,
 };
 
 /* Calibration for HS mode series A/B */
